# 🚨★★★A SHELL SCRIPT WITH CRLF DOES NOT RUN.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is on for this checkout, so git offered to hand
# `.githooks/pre-push` back with Windows line endings — and bash reads the
# trailing `\r` as part of the command, so the very first line becomes
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and the hook dies before it can refuse anything.
# ⛔A gate that silently stops working is worse than no gate: nothing would
# have said so, and a board push would have sailed past the check that exists
# to keep master green.
#
# ⚠️Everything git executes as a script gets the same treatment, not just the
# hook — `tool/*.sh` is run by the merge gate and by the Stop hook.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
